# Pixel Art Rendering Settings

## Required Settings

For pixel art games, always configure PixiJS with these settings:

```typescript
import * as PIXI from 'pixi.js';

// BEFORE creating the engine/app
PIXI.settings.SCALE_MODE = PIXI.SCALE_MODES.NEAREST;
PIXI.settings.ROUND_PIXELS = true;
```

## Why These Settings

- `SCALE_MODE.NEAREST` - Prevents blurry sprites when scaling
- `ROUND_PIXELS` - Prevents sub-pixel rendering artifacts

## Example Usage

```typescript
export class MyPixelArtGame extends ECSExample {
  constructor() {
    // Set pixel art settings FIRST
    PIXI.settings.SCALE_MODE = PIXI.SCALE_MODES.NEAREST;
    PIXI.settings.ROUND_PIXELS = true;

    // Then call super with config
    super({
      width: 320,
      height: 200,
      resolution: 3, // Scale up for crisp pixels
      backgroundColor: 0x000000
    });
  }
}
```

## Common Resolutions

Retro-style games typically use:
- 320×200 (scaled 3x = 960×600) - Classic DOS
- 320×240 (scaled 2x/3x)
- 256×224 (scaled 3x) - NES style
